marta_cust: Hey team — running our nightly embeddings job (50k texts). Seeing intermittent 429s and a couple of "dimension mismatch" responses. Job config: batch_size=512, concurrency=16, model=\"text-embedding-3-large\". Some responses come back 200 with embedding length 1024 but expected 1536. Happens ~15–20 minutes into the run. Example curl + headers below, and one sample response. Any quick ideas?

```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/embeddings \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-cust-ABC" \
  -H "X-Account: acct_ABC123" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"text-embedding-3-large","input":["doc1","doc2"],"batch_size":512}'
```

Sample server log snippet: `HTTP 429 Retry-After: 2` then later `200 OK` with embedding array length 1024 and no error field.

samir_support: Thanks for the signal — can you paste an X-Request-ID from one of the 429/1024 responses and the exact timestamps? Also, are you mixing model names/versions across parallel workers? Two quick asks: 1) account id (you included acct_ABC123 — perfect), 2) a couple of full response headers (the Retry-After is helpful).

marta_cust: Pasted below. Happened at ~2024-11-15T03:22:11Z and ~03:37:40Z. X-Request-ID: req_98765. Headers on a 429: `X-RateLimit-Limit: 1200`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0`, `Retry-After: 2`.

On a 200 that returned 1024 dims the response body starts: { \"data\": [{ \"embedding\": [/* 1024 floats */], \"model\": \"text-embedding-3-large-legacy\" }] } — which surprised us because we requested \"text-embedding-3-large\".

samir_support: That snippet is very helpful. Two quick hypotheses: (A) you're hitting a per-account burst/beta limiter which is returning 429s during spikes, (B) the dim mismatch indicates a fallback/routing to an older model variant (\"-legacy\") on some hosts. For immediate mitigation: decrease concurrency and batch size (try concurrency=4, batch_size=128) and implement exponential backoff with jitter reading the `Retry-After` header. Can you try that and re-run on a subset? Example JS backoff (very small):

```js
async function sendWithBackoff(req) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (attempt < 6) {
    const res = await fetch(req);
    if (res.status === 200) return res.json();
    const ra = parseInt(res.headers.get('Retry-After') || '0', 10);
    const jitter = Math.random() * 1000;
    const wait = Math.min(60000, (Math.pow(2, attempt) * 500) + ra*1000 + jitter);
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait));
    attempt++;
  }
  throw new Error('max attempts');
}
```

leo_infra: Also, can you enable debug-level SDK logs (`REDWOOD_LOG=debug`) and share the per-request `model` field being sent by each worker? I'll correlate with autoscaler and host routing logs for acct_ABC123 around those timestamps.

marta_cust: I re-ran with concurrency=4 & batch=128 on a reduced dataset — completed without 429s and no 1024-dim responses so far. Slower but stable. I still have one saved payload + response showing `model: text-embedding-3-large-legacy` and dims 1024 from earlier. Is caching a possibility? Could a cached/old response get returned?

samir_support: Caching should never change output dimensionality — cache keys include model+version. The `-legacy` model appearing in responses is a big clue: it means requests were routed to a variant we didn't intend. Please also confirm your SDK version — older SDKs may not pin the model alias. If you can, pin the exact model version (e.g., `text-embedding-3-large@v1.3.0`) or use the platform alias that guarantees dims. That avoids accidental routing to legacy variants.

leo_infra: Quick update from infra logs: we traced a small window where one inference host experienced an OOM on the optimized kernel and was auto-failed over to a fallback host running a legacy model variant (which returns 1024-dim embeddings). That same window shows a spike in concurrent connections from acct_ABC123 which likely triggered burst enforcement and some 429s. So there are two correlated issues — routing fallback + burst limiter. We're opening an internal ticket to fix the fallback behavior and ensure model-variant compatibility across hosts.

infra-bot: Ticket INF-2248 created: "Avoid legacy fallback on embedding hosts; ensure variant-dim compatibility" — assigned to eng-runtime. Priority: P1 for correctness in customer workloads.

samir_support: For immediate customer action items (so you can finish your run tonight):
- Keep concurrency <= 4 and batch_size <= 128 for this run (you already tested this).
- Implement the backoff pattern above and always honor `Retry-After`.
- If you need higher throughput, ask for a quota uplift (we can provision a temporary burst increase) or consider Dedicated capacity so you avoid shared burst limits.
- Pin the model version/alias in requests: `model: \"text-embedding-3-large@v1.3.0\"` — that will prevent routing to legacy variants.

marta_cust: Thanks all — reduced config + backoff got the job done for now. Could you share the ETA for the infra fix and whether you'll flip routing for my account temporarily?

leo_infra: We pushed a temporary routing guard for acct_ABC123 to avoid legacy hosts and scheduled the fix rollout. ETA for the rollout is ~6 hours; we'll post back here once the fix is live. In the interim we've applied a temporary quota bump for your account to smooth the job — you should see fewer 429s if you test at moderate concurrency.

marta_cust: Appreciate it. I'll keep the run at the lower settings and re-run a subset once you confirm the rollout. :thumbsup:

samir_support: We'll follow up when INF-2248 is resolved and with confirmation of the rollout. If anything regresses earlier, DM me the req IDs and timestamps and we can escalate.

leo_infra: Follow-up note: after the rollout I will post a short postmortem with root cause and mitigation steps (kernel OOM -> fallback behavior -> routing guard).
